# Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)

Applies to **all** UIs: login, Super Admin, church app, and any later public or member pages. Prefer semantic HTML over clickable `div`s.

## Must

- Every input has a visible `<label>` (or `aria-label`). Errors use `aria-invalid` and are announced.
- Buttons say the action, not only an icon. Icon-only controls need an accessible name.
- Focus visible. Do not remove outlines without a replacement.
- Modals: focus trap, Escape to close, return focus to the opener.
- Color is not the only status signal.
- Images have `alt` (empty `alt=""` if decorative).
- Auth pages: keyboard-complete; errors associated with fields; show/hide password is labeled.
- Tables: column headers, keyboard-reachable row actions (not hover-only).

## Contrast

Text vs background must meet WCAG AA in **both light and dark**. Do not place muted text on canvas/surface if it fails contrast.

If a widget cannot be operated with Tab/Enter/Space, it is not done — including Sign in.
